      "text": "(2) An amount not to exceed two hundred fifty dollars ($250) for each bad faith violation of this section. In determining the amount of the award, the court shall consider proof of matters as justice\nmay require.",
      "source": {
        "path": "pipeline/design/coverage_tracking/fresh_research/sources/CIV_1965.txt",
        "sha256": "9d6628669c233d60147eab4e163a752ffaed6ad34fb9d7a4b8e8a5c0557f3375",
        "start": 4845,
        "end": 5057
      },
      "disposition": "Preserved statutory remedy for bad-faith violation, separately accounted; not part of the selected (e)(1) timing-bearing actual-damages candidate. This remedy does not change the tenant’s eighteen-day request period."
    },
    {
      "text": "(3) The court may award reasonable attorney’s fees and cost to the prevailing party.",
      "source": {
        "path": "pipeline/design/coverage_tracking/fresh_research/sources/CIV_1965.txt",
        "sha256": "9d6628669c233d60147eab4e163a752ffaed6ad34fb9d7a4b8e8a5c0557f3375",
        "start": 5058,
        "end": 5142
      },
      "disposition": "Preserved prevailing-party fee/cost remedy, separately accounted; not part of the selected timing relation and not a change to the tenant’s eighteen-day request period."
    },
    {
      "text": "The D. C. False Claims Act and the tort of wrongful termination each\nhave a three-year statute of limitations that started to run on the day\nArtis lost her job in November 2010. See D. C. Code § 2–381.04(c) (2001)\n(D. C. False Claims Act); Stephenson v. American Dental Assn., 789 A. 2d\n1248, 1249, 1252 (D. C. 2002) (tort of wrongful termination governed by\nthe District's catchall three-year limitations period and claim accrues on\nthe date when plaintiff has unequivocal notice of termination).",
      "source": {
        "path": "pipeline/design/task_evaluation/expansion_sources/ARTIS.txt",
        "sha256": "58a80cda0df64d6ced471014abe7537ac6b136d84dedd5856d49e52ac18ae35a",
        "start": 18309,
        "end": 18806
      },
      "disposition": "Original joint limitation passage preserved. The v3 selected rule concerns wrongful termination only; the D.C. False Claims Act limitation remains research evidence and is not silently negated or treated as an independent tested case."
    }
  ],
